<code>assert element != null => element.equals(this.peek());</code>

Explanation: The comment specifies that if the element is not null, it should be equal to the last element in the queue after the operation. Since `peek()` returns the head of the queue (oldest element), and the queue is circular, the last element added would be the one at the `end` index. However, since `peek()` doesn't directly give the last element, we assume that after adding an element, `peek()` will return the element that was just added if the queue was not full, or the element that replaced the oldest one if it was full. Given the behavior described, `element.equals(this.peek())` captures the essence of the comment.
